{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794596107,"nonce":"wFP8AthdiV1gGcF8lLyyW41ZzrM=","message":"Cooperative completion/fairness checks now drive bounded one-round waits instead of requiring all work to finish within one real-time slice. The helper uses zero-timeout waits and fails after its round limit, while the tests retain their value, ordering, nested-queue and reentrancy assertions. The no-limit budget test checks an immediately ready value, then deliberately spends the slice inside a step and verifies that the wait returns Pending before a second step. It does not assume 500 steps fit in 4 ms or impose a machine-speed upper bound.\n\nAn isolated mutation copy disables local::drive deadline enforcement. The revised budget test then fails promptly: a second poll rejects the task and the assertion sees Rejected instead of Pending. This confirms that the budget assertion remains effective.\n\nCI no longer excludes the four cooperative tests from Miri. The existing -Zmiri-ignore-leaks flag remains for the process-lifetime worker pool. The testing conventions document the bounded-round checks and the budget test. All executable source changes are inside cfg(test); production scheduling, the 4 ms slice, ABI, exports, compilation and linking are unchanged. No unsafe was added.\n\nValidation, under timeouts:\n- macOS arm64: workspace tests, strict Clippy, formatting and diff checks pass. Full Miri passes all 34 future tests with no skips/filters, plus all 35 ABI tests. The future unit suite also passes three repetitions.\n- All nine counter modes pass. CLI and examples pass on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm and Emscripten. C imports pass in every supported mode, with native SQLite where supported. Both native counter bindings pass three repetitions per Ash mode; generated hxcpp and CPPIA pass three times, and generated wasm/Emscripten pass two more times after their initial runs.\n- Linux x86-64 on the NUC: workspace tests, strict Clippy, all native fixture/CLI/example/import modes, generated stock HashLink repetitions and both bindings' Ash-mode repetitions pass. The future unit suite passes three repetitions. Installed the matching Miri and rust-src components and prepared its sysroot; Miri passes all 35 ABI tests and all six focused cooperative checks (including the four previously excluded tests). The full future Miri suite ran on macOS, not Linux. All 179 tracked source files match local SHA-256 hashes after validation; Haxe/hxcpp configuration remains task-local.\n\nNot run: Windows (awaiting commit/push and CI), Linux wasm/Emscripten (both paths ran on macOS), or mobile tests, since this change only affects unit tests, CI and testing conventions and does not change build/link behavior. Optional SQLite is skipped on the NUC because sqlite3.h is absent and by the Emscripten import script.\n\nThe Miri coverage change is uncommitted and not pushed. This issue remains open until it lands.","files":null}]}